x_1 \\
x_2
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
0 \\
0
\end{bmatrix}
\end{equation}

The system of equations is:

\begin{align}
-x_1 + x_2 &= 0 \\
x_1 - x_2 &= 0
\end{align}

These two equations are the same, so we can choose x_1 = 1, and then x_2 = 1. Thus, the eigenvector for λ₁ = 3 is:

\begin{equation}
v_1 = \begin{bmatrix}
1 \\
1
\end{bmatrix}
\end{equation}

For λ₂ = 1:

